      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Subject: Concern Regarding Proposed Sex Education Curriculum  \n\nDear School Board Members,  \n  \nI am writing to formally express my serious concern about the new sex education curriculum being considered, as I believe it oversteps the appropriate boundaries of parental authority over sensitive child education topics. While I appreciate the school's commitment to student well-being, I firmly believe that decisions regarding instruction in sexual education fall within the exclusive domain of parents and guardians, who are best positioned to align teaching content with their family values and legal rights. I urge the board to revise this proposal to include a mandatory opt-out provision or a more robust parental involvement process, ensuring that families retain full control over their children's curriculum choices.  \n\nThank you for your time and attention to this critical matter.  \n\nSincerely,  \n[Your Name]  \n[Your Parent Group/Organization, if applicable]",
